{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.51,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior finding 3","checklist_item":"- [ ] Restore `--no-pull` to the generated help for list/search/ready/show/session-logs/deps (the flag is still accepted at reads_cli.py:602), or enrich the factories so the generator emits it.","criteria":["api-compat"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["Old help documented `--no-pull`, e.g. list: `[--sort=<key>] [--include-archived] [--exclude-deleted] [--no-pull] [--output llm]`; new list usage omits it entirely.","reads_cli.py:602-603: `no_pull = \"--no-pull\" in rest` / `rest = [a for a in rest if a != \"--no-pull\"]` — the flag is still accepted at runtime for every read subcommand.","reads_cli.py:605-606: `if sub not in _NO_PREFETCH: ensure_fresh(tracker, no_sync=no_pull)` — deps is NOT in `_NO_PREFETCH` (=`{\"validate\"}`, reads_cli.py:584), so --no-pull is meaningful for deps too, yet deps help also drops it.","tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py:252-253 exercises `--no-pull` as a live CLI flag.","gen_cli_help.py docstring: 'The package help ... is the CLI's stdout/stderr help contract'."],"finding":"The regenerated help for the read commands (list, search, ready, show, session-logs, deps) drops the documented `--no-pull` flag, but `--no-pull` is still a valid, functioning public CLI flag stripped by the read dispatcher before the subcommand parses. The help/*.txt files are described as the CLI stdout/stderr contract, so a still-accepted flag silently vanishing from documented usage is a help-contract regression.","id":"1","impact":0.36,"location":"docs/cli-reference.md / src/rebar/_cli/help/*.txt","norm_id":"n30b6d4294e6d1374","priority":0.36,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-api-compat","reviewers":["code-review-api-compat"],"scenarios":["A user or script reads `rebar list --help` and no longer sees `--no-pull`, though it still works.","Downstream docs/tooling that mirror the help text drop a still-supported offline flag."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a suppressed-or-visible `--no-pull` argument to the read parser factories (rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reads.py) so the generated help documents the still-accepted flag.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"sometimes","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that a malformed config prefix (`-c` with no value; `--config=badvalue`) is NOT served by the pre-scan and falls through to the real config parser's error path.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["_help_route.py:118-130: \"Returns ``None`` when the prefix is malformed (a missing or non ``SECTION.KEY=VALUE`` value) so the real config parser in ``_main_dispatch`` produces its exact error rather than the pre-scan guessing at a help form.\"","_help_route.py:120-129: `while out and (out[0] in (\"-c\", \"--config\") ...): ... if not _valid_override(value): return None`","test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py:161: only `_cli.main([\"-c\", \"ticket.default_assignee=x@y\", \"create\", \"--help\"])` — the well-formed prefix; no case for `-c` with no value or `-c notavalue`","ABSENCE: search for `--config=` and `config prefix` in tests/ returns only the single well-formed b8de case; no test asserts the malformed-prefix fall-through emits the real parser's error and does not serve help/overview"],"finding":"The new malformed-config-prefix fall-through branch in `_help_route._strip_config_prefix` (returns None for a missing value or a value that is not `SECTION.KEY=VALUE`, so the pre-scan defers to the real config parser's exact error rather than serving a help form) has no test. The b8de contract test only exercises the well-formed prefix `-c ticket.default_assignee=x@y`.","id":"3","impact":0.27,"location":"src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:112","norm_id":"n1b9c5c605c3c0095","priority":0.27,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["`rebar -c` (dangling config flag with no value)","`rebar --config=notavalidoverride create` (value lacking `SECTION.KEY=VALUE` shape)"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a parametrized case in test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py (or a unit test loading _help_route) asserting `_help_route.pre_scan([\"-c\", \"create\", \"--help\"])` and `_help_route.pre_scan([\"--config=bad\", \"create\", \"--help\"])` both return None (fall-through), rather than serving help/overview.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"n