arated `rebar list --status open` is rejected as an unknown option. The generated help documents a grammar the runtime rejects.","id":"2","impact":0.0,"location":"src/rebar/_cli/help/list.txt / docs/cli-reference.md","norm_id":"n5725179c36914201","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","reviewer_id":"code-review-api-compat","reviewers":["code-review-api-compat"],"scenarios":["A user copies the space form from `rebar list --help` (`--status open`) and gets an unknown-option error.","LLM/agent tooling parses the new usage string and emits the space form, breaking `list` invocations."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"none","escapes_automation":false,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the help-backed advanced factories (audit/metrics/bridge/bridge_arms) render at the fixed 80-column width (use RebarHelpFormatter or a width-pinned formatter) so generated artifacts are reproducible and --check is COLUMNS-independent.","criteria":["correctness","regression","edge-cases"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":"novelty-region","evidence":["src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/audit.py:23: `formatter_class=argparse.HelpFormatter,`","src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/metrics.py:23: `formatter_class=argparse.HelpFormatter,`","src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py:50-71 `RebarHelpFormatter` hardcodes `width=_FIXED_WIDTH` (80) precisely because argparse's default 'reads shutil.get_terminal_size() (honouring COLUMNS) when width is None, which makes help non-reproducible'","scripts/gen_cli_help.py docstring: 'formatting its --help at the fixed S2a width' and 'a non-deterministic second render' is a --check failure","gen_cli_help.py:_help_backed treats group != 'intercept' as help-backed, so audit/metrics (group='static_read') and bridge/bridge-fsck/bridge-probe are all rendered into committed .txt artifacts","_determinism_failures (gen_cli_help.py:131-134) re-renders in the same process/terminal, so it cannot catch COLUMNS-driven divergence — only a --check run under a different COLUMNS width would fail as 'stale artifacts'"],"finding":"The help-backed advanced-family parser factories (audit, metrics, bridge, bridge-fsck, bridge-probe) render with the stdlib argparse.HelpFormatter (terminal/COLUMNS-width dependent) instead of the fixed-width RebarHelpFormatter, so their generated help artifacts are not reproducible across environments — contradicting the documented fixed-80-column invariant that scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check relies on.","id":"0","impact":0.36,"location":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/audit.py:23","norm_id":"nb8bd7eb556b81a6e","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.36,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"For the help-backed factories, either default formatter_class to RebarHelpFormatter, or have gen_cli_help.py force a fixed width during render (e.g.